            <ArticleTitle>Surgically Treated Pelvic Pain Caused by Nutcracker Syndrome and Worsened by Cockett Syndrome in a Child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>422.e15-422.e17</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0890-5096(17)30692-1</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.avsg.2017.05.005</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Nutcracker syndrome is rarely seen in the young. Most of the symptoms regress during follow-up. Rarely surgical intervention is necessary. This case presentation is unique for being the first case of nutcracker syndrome and coexistent Cockett syndrome that is treated with surgical intervention.</AbstractText>
